.TH CGFREECELL 6 "November 2026" "cggames 1.4.0"
.SH NAME
cgfreecell \- the FreeCell patience
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cgfreecell
.RI [ "toolkit options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cgfreecell
plays FreeCell as Windows plays it.
The table is empty until a game is dealt with
.B New Game
or
.BR "Select Game" .
The whole pack is dealt face up into eight columns.
Build the four suits up from their aces on the home cells at the top
right to win.
.PP
The top card of a column can go on one a rank higher of the other
colour, into an empty column, into one of the four free cells at the
top left, which hold a card each, or home.
A card in a free cell can go on a column or home.
Cards are moved one at a time, but a run down in alternate colours
is moved for you a card at a time through the free cells and empty
columns, when there are enough of them: one more card than there are
empty free cells, twice that for each empty column, one fewer of those
if the run goes to one.
.PP
Click a column or a free cell, which shows its card picked, then the
place it is to go: as many cards go as can.
A place the cards picked up can go to is ringed in yellow while the
pointer is over it.
Click it again to put it down.
When a run could go into an empty column, you are asked whether to
move the column, as much of it as can go, or a single card.
A double click on a column sends its card to a free cell.
Holding the right button on a card in a column shows it whole.
Cards that nothing could want to go on any more go home by themselves.
The king between the cells looks towards the pointer while it is level
with him, and towards the cells a card has just gone to; he smiles at a
win.
.PP
Each deal has a number, shown in the title, from 1 to 1000000, the
same deals as Windows' FreeCell has for those numbers.
.B New Game
deals one at random,
.B Select Game
the one asked for, and
.B Restart Game
the same one again.
.B Undo
takes back the last move.
The menu bar shows the cards still to go home.
.PP
A game ends when it is won, or lost when no move is left.
A game given up once a move is made, by dealing another or by leaving
the program, counts as lost; you are asked first.
.B Statistics
shows the games won and lost, in this session and in all, and the
longest runs of each.
.PP
The cards are drawn as large as the window lets the table be, larger
or smaller with it, down to three quarters of their usual size; a
window wider than the table needs spreads the columns apart.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B Display messages on illegal moves
Says so when cards clicked on can't go where the next click is.
.TP
.B Quick play (no animation)
Moves the cards at once, without showing them go.
.TP
.B Double-click moves card to free cell
As it says; otherwise a double click picks a column up and puts it
down again.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cggames/cgfreecell.conf
The options, the statistics, and the size of the window.
.PP
Without the variable,
.I ~/.config
is used.
.SH AUTHORS
cgfreecell is Freecell from gnome-games 1.4, ported to CGTK, and made
to play as Windows' FreeCell does.
Changwoo Ryu wrote Freecell.
Its card faces, and the king between the cells, the king of spades',
are drawn from a public domain deck, in SVG.
